# Architecture — layers

See [`architecture/general.mdc`](./general.mdc) for the import flow and cross-cutting rules.

## `1_app` — `~app`, layer `app`

Application initialization — the root that wires everything together.

- Lives here: providers (theme, router, query client, MobX, UI kit), global styles (`index.css`), the root render entry (`index.tsx`), app-wide store setup.
- Structure: segment-based, no slices — `providers/`, `styles/`, `config/`, plus the `index.tsx` entry. Capture is `segment`.
- May import: everything below it (all layers). Nothing imports `app`.
- Public API: `index.ts` re-exports the entry/providers upper layers need.

## `2_pages` — `~pages`, layer `pages`

Page-level composition for a route.

- Lives here: one PascalCase slice per route. No business logic — only composition and route-bound wiring.
- Structure: flat slice. Files: `<Name>.page.tsx`, `<Name>.page.m.css`, optional `<Name>.page.skeleton.tsx`, `index.ts`. Etalon: `src/2_pages/Auth`. Capture is `page`.
- May import: widgets, modules, core, shared, global. Not `app`. Not other pages.
- Cross-import between pages is forbidden.

## `3_widgets` — `~widgets`, layer `widgets`

Compositional blocks combining modules into self-sufficient chunks used by pages.

- Lives here: UI sections too composed to be a single module — header, dashboards, sidebars.
- Structure: slice-based, PascalCase directory. Simple widgets are **flat** (no segment folders): `<Name>.component.tsx`, `<Name>.vm.ts`, `<Name>.component.m.css`, `index.ts`. Etalon: `src/3_widgets/Header`. Add `presentation/`/`model/` only when the widget outgrows that. Capture is `widget`.
- May import: modules, core, shared, global. Not pages. Not `app`. Not other widgets.
- Public API via `index.ts`.

## `4_modules` — `~modules`, layer `modules`

Business modules — self-contained slices delivering a piece of business value: user scenarios (login, add-to-cart, filter) and domain models (user, product, order). A module owns its UI, use-cases, domain rules, and API.

- Lives here: a user-facing scenario and/or a domain model with presentation, interactors, data, and domain. Self-contained.
- Structure: slice-based, PascalCase directory. Segments `presentation`, `model`, `data`, `domain` as needed (`lib`/`config`/`constants` only when used). Etalon: `src/4_modules/Auth`. Capture is `module`.
  - `domain` imports nothing (enforced by `no-restricted-imports`). No segment barrels — files are imported by path (`../model/Otp.interactor`).
- May import: core, shared, global. Not widgets/pages/app. Not other modules (cross-slice imports forbidden).
- Public API via `index.ts` (re-export the presentation entry, e.g. `AuthWizard`).

## `5_core` — `~core`, layer `core`

Project-scoped infrastructure wired once and consumed by upper layers.

- Lives here: the API client instance, store setup, cross-cutting services and app-wide domain objects (auth, user, session) that are app-wide but not UI.
- Structure: segment-based, no slices — `api/`, `auth/`, `session/`, `lib/`, etc. Capture is `segment`.
- May import: shared, global. Not modules/widgets/pages/app.
- Public API via `index.ts`.

## `6_shared` — `~shared`, layer `shared`

Reusable code with no business meaning — UI kit, utils, types, configs, constants.

- Lives here: the design system (UI-kit components), generic hooks, formatters, generic types, icons, config. No domain knowledge.
- Structure: segment-based, no slices — `ui/`, `lib/`, `config/`, `constants/`, `types/`. Capture is `segment`.
- May import: global only. Nothing above it.
- Public API via `index.ts`.

## `7_global` — `~global`, layer `global`

Global abstractions applied across the entire app — project-wide types, styles, polyfills.

- Lives here: ambient declarations (`modules.d.ts`, `react.utilities.d.ts`), global type augmentations, polyfills. No runtime business code.
- Structure: flat files, no entry-point enforcement. Capture is `segment`.
- May import: nothing from the app (it's the foundation) — external libs only.
